      "source_line": "| 1788 | 11000165 / AMR-109-0165 | Problem 2.8 \u2014 Recall that we noted, earlier, that every genus g Heegaard splitting of every homology 3-sphere is obtained by allowi\u2026 | 0.0540 | 5.5 | 3 | unknown | claimed_solved | 1/5 |  | Accepted explicit, generally infinite algebraic generating families for both closed HI_g and HK_g for every g>=2: balanced disk corrections in genus two; Omori conjugacy and lattice-Schreier families for g>=3. Application of established theory; no novelty, finite-generation, or stronger short geometric-generator claim. Separate infinite-index meridian obstruction addresses Holden 2607.07587v1 Conjecture 7.1, not an unconditional theorem. [Reader](attempts/11000165/public/README.md); [independent public review](attempts/11000165/independent_public_review/ACCEPTANCE_REPORT.md). |  |",
